course: dictionary
lesson: 9909
title: A word from the past: tallyman
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a time long ago, or to one place. You can often work them out from the words around them. «Tallymen are party helpers who watch the Irish count and keep their own tally to guess the result early.» Tally means a count, so a tallyman is someone who keeps count.
explain: Look at the clues: party helpers, watch the count, keep their own tally, guess the result early. These all point to counting, not to a person who sells things. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Tallymen are party helpers who keep their own count" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: The word has a second, older meaning too. In old UK stories, the tallyman was a door-to-door salesman who collected small weekly payments. The clues are «came round» and money. Today people more often say counter or collector.
fact: A tally is a count, or a record of how many things there are.
fact: A tallyman was a person who kept a tally of goods, such as bananas loaded onto a ship, or votes.
fact: In the «Banana Boat Song», the singer asks, «Come, Mister Tally Man, tally me banana», meaning count my bananas.
fact: In old UK stories, a tallyman was a door-to-door salesman who sold goods and collected small weekly payments.
fact: Today people more often say «counter» or «collector» instead of tallyman.
exercise: «Tallymen are party helpers who watch the Irish count and keep their own tally to guess the result early.» What does tally mean here? | A kind of cheap biscuit | A loud shout of joy | A party game with balloons | *A count of things, such as votes
exercise: In the Banana Boat Song, what is the tallyman doing? | *Counting bunches of bananas being loaded | Eating bananas on a ship | Singing about the sea | Selling bananas door to door
exercise: In old UK stories, the tallyman «came round» on Fridays. What did he come to do? | Sweep the path | *Collect small weekly payments | Give out prizes | Deliver the post
test: Which word do people more often use today instead of tallyman? | Painter | Captain | *Collector | Baker
test: In an old UK story, what does «the tallyman came round» suggest? | A ship sailed into the harbour | A party had just started | *A salesman came to the door to collect payments | A child was lost in the woods
exam: Jayden reads, «The tallyman kept a tally of the votes.» What does tallyman most likely mean? | *A person who counts | A ship's captain | A party guest | A kind of banana
